# This CITATION.cff file enables the "Cite this repository" button on GitHub.
# 本文件驱动 GitHub 仓库首页的"Cite this repository"按钮。
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  如果您在学术研究、教学或工程中使用了本技能，请引用本仓库。
  If you use this skill in your research, teaching or work, please cite it.
title: monograph-writing
authors:
  - name: newdeme
    website: "https://github.com/newdeme"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/newdeme/monograph-writing"
abstract: >-
  A batch-writing pipeline for academic monographs and long-form books,
  packaged as an Agent Skill for AI writing assistants. It turns book
  writing into small verifiable batches: a progress ledger persists all
  state on disk for seamless continuation across sessions and co-authors;
  an academic red-line system forbids fabricated references and restricts
  citations to the author's own evidence corpus (AI knowledge base, Zotero,
  or an in-project folder of any file format); and four validation scripts
  automatically check citation numbering, word-count tiers, and
  figure/table numbering before each batch closes, then generate stripped
  clean copies and a fully-styled merged Word manuscript.
keywords:
  - academic-writing
  - monograph
  - AI-assisted-writing
  - agent-skills
  - writing-pipeline
  - citation-validation
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.2.1
date-released: "2026-08-19"
